\id BAK
\h The Order of Reading the Psalter
\toc1 The Order of Reading the Psalter
\toc2 The Order of the Psalter
\toc3 Psalter
\mt1 The Order of Reading the Psalter
\p The Psalter is divided into twenty Kathismata. It is read through once each week outside Great Lent and twice each week during Great Lent.
\s1 Outside Great Lent
\tr \th1 Day \th2 Matins \th3 Vespers
\tr \tc1 Sunday \tc2 II, III\f + \ft The Psalter is read neither at Vespers on Sunday evening nor on a feast of the Lord that has a Vigil. For the Third Kathisma of Sunday Matins, the Seventeenth Kathisma of the Psalter is read, unless a Vigil or a celebrated Saint calls for the Polyeleos in its place. On the other days of the week a Vigil or a celebrated Saint likewise has the Polyeleos (Psalms 134 and 135), with the verses appointed by the Eclogarion for the feast.\f* \tc3
\tr \tc1 Monday \tc2 IV, V \tc3 VI
\tr \tc1 Tuesday \tc2 VII, VIII \tc3 IX
\tr \tc1 Wednesday \tc2 X, XI \tc3 XII
\tr \tc1 Thursday \tc2 XIII, XIV \tc3 XV
\tr \tc1 Friday \tc2 XIX, XX \tc3 XVIII
\tr \tc1 Saturday \tc2 XVI, XVII \tc3 I
\s1 The First, Second, Third, Fourth, and Sixth Weeks of Great Lent
\tr \th1 Day \th2 Matins \th3 First Hour \th4 Third Hour \th5 Sixth Hour \th6 Ninth Hour \th7 Vespers
\tr \tc1 Sunday \tc2 II, III\f + \ft In Greek usage the Seventeenth Kathisma (Psalm 118) or the Polyeleos is chanted, as appointed by the Typicon.\f* \tc3 \tc4 \tc5 \tc6 \tc7
\tr \tc1 Monday \tc2 IV, V, VI \tc3 \tc4 VII \tc5 VIII \tc6 IX \tc7 XVIII
\tr \tc1 Tuesday \tc2 X, XI, XII \tc3 XIII \tc4 XIV \tc5 XV \tc6 XVI \tc7 XVIII
\tr \tc1 Wednesday \tc2 XIX, XX, I \tc3 II \tc4 III \tc5 IV \tc6 V \tc7 XVIII
\tr \tc1 Thursday \tc2 VI, VII, VIII \tc3 IX \tc4 X \tc5 XI \tc6 XII \tc7 XVIII
\tr \tc1 Friday \tc2 XIII, XIV, XV \tc3 \tc4 XIX \tc5 XX \tc6 \tc7 XVIII
\tr \tc1 Saturday \tc2 XVI, XVII \tc3 \tc4 \tc5 \tc6 \tc7 I
\s1 The Fifth Week of Great Lent
\tr \th1 Day \th2 Matins \th3 First Hour \th4 Third Hour \th5 Sixth Hour \th6 Ninth Hour \th7 Vespers
\tr \tc1 Sunday \tc2 II, III \tc3 \tc4 \tc5 \tc6 \tc7
\tr \tc1 Monday \tc2 IV, V, VI \tc3 \tc4 VII \tc5 VIII \tc6 IX \tc7 X
\tr \tc1 Tuesday \tc2 XI, XII, XIII \tc3 XIV \tc4 XV \tc5 XVI \tc6 XVIII \tc7 XIX
\tr \tc1 Wednesday \tc2 XX, I, II \tc3 III \tc4 IV \tc5 V \tc6 VI \tc7 VII
\tr \tc1 Thursday \tc2 VIII \tc3 \tc4 IX \tc5 X \tc6 XI \tc7 XII
\tr \tc1 Friday \tc2 XIII, XIV, XV \tc3 \tc4 XIX \tc5 XX \tc6 \tc7 XVIII
\tr \tc1 Saturday \tc2 XVI, XVII \tc3 \tc4 \tc5 \tc6 \tc7 I
\s1 The Fifth Week of Great Lent, When the Annunciation Falls on Thursday
\p The Great Canon is chanted on the Tuesday of the week.
\tr \th1 Day \th2 Matins \th3 First Hour \th4 Third Hour \th5 Sixth Hour \th6 Ninth Hour \th7 Vespers
\tr \tc1 Sunday \tc2 II, III, XVII \tc3 \tc4 \tc5 \tc6 \tc7
\tr \tc1 Monday \tc2 IV, V, VI \tc3 VII \tc4 VIII \tc5 IX \tc6 X \tc7 XI
\tr \tc1 Tuesday \tc2 XII \tc3 \tc4 XIII \tc5 XIV \tc6 XV \tc7 XVI
\tr \tc1 Wednesday \tc2 XIX, XX, I \tc3 II \tc4 III \tc5 IV \tc6 V \tc7
\tr \tc1 Thursday \tc2 VI, VII, VIII\f + \ft On the Thursday of the Annunciation, the Polyeleos (Psalm 44) is chanted at the Third Kathisma of Matins.\f* \tc3 IX \tc4 X \tc5 XI \tc6 XII \tc7
\tr \tc1 Friday \tc2 XIII, XIV, XV \tc3 \tc4 XIX \tc5 XX \tc6 \tc7 XVIII
\tr \tc1 Saturday \tc2 XVI, XVII \tc3 \tc4 \tc5 \tc6 \tc7 I
\s1 Holy Week\f + \ft The Psalter is not read from Holy Thursday until Vespers on the Saturday of Renewal Week, at which point it is resumed.\f*
\tr \th1 Day \th2 Matins \th3 First Hour \th4 Third Hour \th5 Sixth Hour \th6 Ninth Hour \th7 Vespers
\tr \tc1 Sunday \tc2 II, III \tc3 \tc4 \tc5 \tc6 \tc7
\tr \tc1 Monday \tc2 IV, V, VI \tc3 \tc4 VII \tc5 VIII \tc6 \tc7 XVIII
\tr \tc1 Tuesday \tc2 IX, X, XI \tc3 \tc4 XII \tc5 XIII \tc6 \tc7 XVIII
\tr \tc1 Wednesday \tc2 XIV, XV, XVI \tc3 \tc4 XIX \tc5 XX \tc6 \tc7 XVIII
\tr \tc1 Thursday \tc2 \tc3 \tc4 \tc5 \tc6 \tc7
\tr \tc1 Friday \tc2 \tc3 \tc4 \tc5 \tc6 \tc7
\tr \tc1 Saturday \tc2 XVII \tc3 \tc4 \tc5 \tc6 \tc7
\p Each Kathisma is divided into three Stases. After the First and the Second Stasis:
\pm Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit; both now and ever, and unto the ages of ages. Amen.
\pm Alleluia, Alleluia, Alleluia. Glory to Thee, O God. (\it Thrice\it*)
\pm Lord, have mercy. (\it Thrice\it*)
\pm Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit; both now and ever, and unto the ages of ages. Amen.
\p After the Third Stasis, at the end of the Kathisma:
\pm Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit; both now and ever, and unto the ages of ages. Amen.
\pm Alleluia, Alleluia, Alleluia. Glory to Thee, O God. (\it Twice\it*)
\pm Alleluia, Alleluia, Alleluia. Glory to Thee, O God our Hope, O Lord, glory be to Thee.
